{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Com[Bb]panion raised his hand against his friends
Vi[Eb]olated the covenant he made
[Bb]Speech smoother than butter to the eye
War was hidden deep [Eb]inside
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Gm]Words softer than oil [F]on the tongue
[Eb]Yet drawn swords were [Bb]waiting there
[Gm]They have no fear [F]of God in their hearts
And they [Eb]never change their [F]ways
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Cast your burden on the LORD
[Eb]He will sustain you forever
[Gm]He will never let the righteous be shaken
When the [Eb]trouble starts to [F][Bb]grow
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
God will hear and humble them
Who are ent[Eb]hroned from of old
[Bb]Men of blood and treachery
Will not live out [Eb]half their [Eb/F]days
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Cast your burden on the LORD
[Eb]He will sustain you forever
[Gm]He will never let the righteous be shaken
When [Eb]the trouble starts [F]to grow
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]You will bring them down to [F]the pit
To the place of de[Eb]struction
But I will trust in you alone
In [F]your endless protec[Bb]tion
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Cast your burden on the LORD
[Eb]He will sustain you forever
[Gm]He will never let the righteous be shaken
When [Eb]the trouble starts [F]to [Bb]grow
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Cast your burden on the LORD
[Eb]He will sustain you
{end_of_verse}

